---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
---

<style>
  section {
    padding-block: 2rem 3rem;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    margin: 3rem 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .intro {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  .fm-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 0 0 2.5rem;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .fm-links a {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .fm-links a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  /* ---- system diagram --------------------------------------------- */

  .arch-diagram {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 0.4rem 1rem;
    align-items: stretch;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .arch-box {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    background: var(--color-bg-alt);
  }

  .arch-box strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  .arch-box span {
    display: block;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    margin-top: 0.2rem;
  }

  .arch-box-accent {
    border-color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .arch-arrow {
    text-align: center;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .arch-span-2 {
    grid-column: span 2;
  }

  .arch-span-3 {
    grid-column: span 3;
  }

  @media (max-width: 40rem) {
    .arch-diagram {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .arch-box,
    .arch-arrow {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }

  /* ---- component / security cards ----------------------------------- */

  .card-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(16rem, 1fr));
    gap: 1.25rem;
  }

  .card {
    padding: 1.25rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
  }

  .card h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .card p {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0;
  }

  ul.security-list {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  ul.security-list li {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
  }

  ul.security-list strong {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  /* ---- deploy pipeline ------------------------------------------------ */

  .pipeline {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    align-items: center;
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }

  .pipeline-step {
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.4rem 0.9rem;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    background: var(--color-bg-alt);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .pipeline-arrow {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  /* ---- access tiers table ---------------------------------------------- */

  .table-scroll {
    overflow-x: auto;
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
  }

  table {
    border-collapse: collapse;
    width: 100%;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    min-width: 40rem;
  }

  th,
  td {
    text-align: left;
    padding: 0.65rem 0.9rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    vertical-align: top;
  }

  thead th {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
  }

  tbody tr:last-child td {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  td:first-child,
  th:first-child {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>

<Layout
  title="Architecture | File Manager | 7 Beacons"
  description="How the gcs-fileserver file manager is built: public browsing, admin controls, and AI agent integration sharing one storage backend."
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="container">
      <h1>How the File Manager works</h1>
      <p class="intro">
        A small, real system with three separate audiences — a public visitor, an admin, and a
        connected AI agent — sharing one storage backend, each through a different door with
        different keys.
      </p>
      <p class="fm-links">
        <a href="/fm">→ Browse the File Manager</a>
        <a href="/admin?tab=files">→ Admin login</a>
      </p>

      <h2>System overview</h2>
      <div class="arch-diagram">
        <div class="arch-box">
          <strong>Public visitor</strong>
          <span>Browser, no login</span>
        </div>
        <div class="arch-box">
          <strong>Admin</strong>
          <span>Browser, logged in</span>
        </div>
        <div class="arch-box arch-box-accent">
          <strong>AI agent</strong>
          <span>MCP client</span>
        </div>

        <div class="arch-arrow">↓</div>
        <div class="arch-arrow">↓</div>
        <div class="arch-arrow">↓</div>

        <div class="arch-box arch-span-2">
          <strong>7 Beacons — this site</strong>
          <span>Astro, static · /fm, admin controls live at /admin</span>
        </div>
        <div class="arch-box arch-box-accent">
          <strong>Model Context Protocol</strong>
          <span>Direct connection, bearer token — never touches this site</span>
        </div>

        <div class="arch-arrow arch-span-3">↓</div>

        <div class="arch-box arch-span-3">
          <strong>mcp-fileserver backend</strong>
          <span>Python (Starlette), containerized, its own Cloud Run service</span>
          <span>Public read API · Admin API (session + CSRF) · MCP tool surface (bearer token)</span>
        </div>

        <div class="arch-arrow arch-span-3">↓</div>

        <div class="arch-box arch-span-3">
          <strong>Google Cloud Storage bucket</strong>
          <span>files/ — browsable content · _admin/ — runtime config (2FA secret, password-reset override), outside the browsable prefix so it can never appear in a listing</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Components</h2>
      <div class="card-grid">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Frontend</h3>
          <p>
            This site: Astro, statically rendered, ships close to zero JS by default. The file
            explorer itself is a small React island, hydrated only on the two /fm pages — the
            rest of the site stays untouched.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Backend</h3>
          <p>
            A separate service, mcp-fileserver: Python on Starlette, its own container, its own
            repo and deploy pipeline. It's the only thing that talks to storage directly, and it
            exposes three independent APIs on top of it.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Storage</h3>
          <p>
            One Google Cloud Storage bucket holds everything. A path prefix separates
            world-browsable content from a small amount of runtime config the admin panel needs
            to mutate without a redeploy.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>AI agent integration</h3>
          <p>
            The backend also speaks the Model Context Protocol: a fixed, small tool surface — read
            a file, list files, write a text file, create a share link — for a connected AI agent,
            authenticated with its own bearer token, entirely separate from the admin login.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>CI/CD</h3>
          <p>
            Both repos deploy via GitHub Actions: type-check, build, containerize, push to
            Artifact Registry, deploy to Cloud Run. GitHub authenticates to Google Cloud via
            Workload Identity Federation — no long-lived key stored anywhere.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Three doors, three keys</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th></th>
              <th>Public visitor</th>
              <th>Admin</th>
              <th>AI agent</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td>Entry point</td>
              <td>/fm</td>
              <td>/admin</td>
              <td>MCP tool calls</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Authentication</td>
              <td>None</td>
              <td>Email + password, optional TOTP 2FA, server-side session</td>
              <td>Bearer token</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Can do</td>
              <td>Browse and download public files</td>
              <td>Upload, organize, delete, hide/unhide files, manage its own login</td>
              <td>Read a file, list files, write a text file, create a share link</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td>Can't do</td>
              <td>See admin-only files — a hidden file returns the exact same 404 as one that doesn't exist</td>
              <td>—</td>
              <td>Touch visibility rules, upload binary files, or manage admin auth</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <ul class="security-list">
        <li><strong>Password hashing:</strong> scrypt, a memory-hard algorithm — not a bare hash — with a random salt per password.</li>
        <li><strong>Real sessions:</strong> server-side and revocable, not a signed token that stays valid on its own until it expires.</li>
        <li><strong>CSRF protection:</strong> every admin write requires a custom header on top of the session cookie, backed by a strict CORS origin allowlist.</li>
        <li><strong>Brute-force lockout:</strong> repeated failed logins trigger an escalating delay — 15s, 30s, 60s… capped at 15 minutes.</li>
        <li><strong>Two-factor authentication:</strong> optional TOTP, works with any standard authenticator app.</li>
        <li><strong>Email-based password reset:</strong> single-use, 30-minute links; an identical response either way so the system never reveals whether an email address is the real admin account; a successful reset logs out every existing session but never touches 2FA, so a compromised inbox alone still isn't enough to get in.</li>
        <li><strong>No existence leaks:</strong> hidden files are invisible, not just unlisted — a direct request for one returns the same response as a file that was never there.</li>
        <li><strong>No secrets in git:</strong> every credential is generated locally, gitignored, and deployed as an environment variable — never committed.</li>
        <li><strong>No long-lived cloud keys:</strong> both repos' GitHub Actions authenticate to Google Cloud via Workload Identity Federation, impersonating a scoped service account per run.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Deploy pipeline</h2>
      <p class="intro">Every push runs CI; every merge to main ships automatically.</p>
      <div class="pipeline">
        <span class="pipeline-step">Push / PR</span>
        <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
        <span class="pipeline-step">CI: type-check + build</span>
        <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
        <span class="pipeline-step">Merge to main</span>
        <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
        <span class="pipeline-step">Build container</span>
        <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
        <span class="pipeline-step">Push to Artifact Registry</span>
        <span class="pipeline-arrow">→</span>
        <span class="pipeline-step">Deploy to Cloud Run</span>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
